  "notes": "Modified cash basis village. Governmental lines from the governmental funds statement, 2022 Total Governmental Funds column (pp4-5); it rolls fund balances 574,505 -> 655,044 (fund balance fields). Ending cash 1,100,166 is the governmental funds Cash line (p3); beginning cash 1,080,312 is the printed 2021 comparative column (p3). Business-type (Water, Sewer) lines from the modified cash proprietary statement (p7), which ties to the Statement of Activities (p2): operating revenues 225,699, expenses 283,332 + interest 3,545 = 286,877 (p2 total business-type expenses); net position 1,244,737 -> 1,183,559. Proprietary cash flow statement (p8) not recorded (as later years; non-GAAP). Balance sheet from the government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1) because its governmental column carries internal balances (-455,061) that the governmental funds statement shows gross (due from/to other funds); totals from the 2022 Total column. Detail: budgetary comparison schedules for all funds (pp9-15); 'Total available resources' lines include the beginning balance and are not recorded; funds with a single line per section have no printed total. Zero-actual lines with budgets recorded with amount 0. Grant revenue 51,592 has no grantor printed (generic Grants). Read pages 1-15 of 15"
